  "raw": {
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/assistant-associate-professor-master-of-physician-assistant-studies-program/": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor — Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor — Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Assistant/Associate Professor — Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences at Mary Baldwin University invites applications for a 12-month full-time, renewable (Clinical or Scholar Pathway) Physician Assistant Faculty position beginning in September 2026. Position Summary: The Physician Assistant (MSPA) Program is fully accredited, and the dynamic faculty teaches within a unique interprofessional curriculum. We invite individuals with exceptional skills and experience in contemporary medical practice, teaching, and administration to apply. Primary responsibilities include guiding students through the PA program through teaching, advising, and mentorship. Teaching load will be determined according to expertise and program/ college needs. Candidates should be dynamic and dedicated educators who will facilitate classroom and applied learning activities while fostering an inclusive and caring learning environment. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, university, community, and professional service, and supporting the interprofessional education curriculum. Required Qualifications Master’s degree required. Must possess an unencumbered PA, NP, DO, or MD license to practice in the Commonwealth of Virginia. A minimum of 3 years of clinical experience as a Physician Assistant Strong communication, teamwork, & interpersonal skills Prefer red Qualifications Prior teaching experience is preferred, but not required Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University values and celebrates diversity, is committed to equal opportunity, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, or veteran’s status. All correspondence relating to the position of PA Faculty should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Administration & Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled.  The projected start date is fall semester, 2026. Salary range is $90,000 – $105,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/full-time-faculty-family-nurse-practitioner-program-clinical-education-coordinator-assistant-associate-professor/": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty: Family Nurse Practitioner Program – Clinical Education Coordinator (Assistant/Associate Professor)",
      "description": "Full-Time Faculty: Family Nurse Practitioner Program – Clinical Education Coordinator (Assistant/Associate Professor) — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Full-Time Faculty: Family Nurse Practitioner Program – Clinical Education Coordinator (Assistant/Associate Professor) Position Summary: This is a 12-month, full-time Clinical Faculty position in the Family Nurse Practitioner Program for the School of Nursing in the Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences for the start of the 2026-2027 academic year. The position is hybrid with physical work location at Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences, Fishersville, VA campus. This faculty member will be responsible for teaching didactic and clinical courses within the FNP curriculum; participating in curriculum development, review, and evaluation; and mentoring and advising graduate nursing students. This faculty member will contribute to the ongoing assessment processes necessary to maintain compliance with CCNE accreditation standards. Required Qualifications Candidates must have earned a Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP), Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Nursing, or a related doctoral degree from an accredited institution. Candidates with a Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) will be considered based on exceptional clinical experience, demonstrated expertise in advanced practice nursing, and a strong commitment to nursing education. Must be a nationally certified and state-licensed Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP-BC or FNP-C), with current or eligible licensure in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Minimum of three years of clinical practice experience as a Family Nurse Practitioner in a primary care or related setting. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively mentor and advise a diverse student population. Prior didactic teaching experience in a graduate nursing program is preferred; experience teaching in a Family Nurse Practitioner or other advanced practice nursing program is highly desirable. Familiarity with online and hybrid instructional delivery methods, including the use of learning management systems (e.g., Canvas), video conferencing, and other educational technologies. Experience with or understanding of simulation-based learning and curriculum development for experiential learning environments. Demonstrated commitment to learner-centered education, evidence-based teaching practices, and innovative approaches to nursing education. Prefer red Qualifications Prior experience teaching at the graduate level is preferred. Experience with online and hybrid education delivery, including the use of learning management systems and virtual instructional tools, is highly desirable. Familiarity with instructional design, student assessment, and use of technology in nursing education is highly desirable. Formal education or training in teaching, instructional technology, curriculum development, or clinical precepting (such as through a nurse educator certificate or completion of faculty development workshops) is a plus. Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University is committed to promoting a culture of equity and inclusion among students, staff, and faculty. The university does not discriminate on the basis sex, gender, nor does the university discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, color, age, disability, religion, veteran’s status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. All correspondence relating to the position of FT FNP Faculty and Clinical Education Coordinator should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 Cc: hr@marybaldwin.edu A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled. Annual salary is $100,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/occupational-therapy-primary-faculty/": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty",
      "description": "Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty Position Summary: Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences welcomes applications for the Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty position with an anticipated start of January 2027. This position is responsible for teaching and managing a discipline-appropriate course load using contemporary, inclusive instructional strategies and technology to support student learning and engagement. Faculty develop and maintain course materials, assess student performance fairly and consistently, mentor and advise students, and support doctoral capstone experiences. The role includes active participation in program operations, accreditation activities, recruitment, curriculum development, committee service, and collaboration with community and professional partners to support continuous program improvement. Faculty are expected to maintain professional standards through ongoing scholarship, professional development, and involvement in professional organizations while serving as positive role model for students and colleagues. Additional responsibilities include supporting college and program initiatives, maintaining accurate records and confidentiality, participating in institutional events, and performing other duties as assigned by the Program Director. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree required in occupational therapy or related field of study National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy State licensure Three years’ experience as an occupational therapist in an occupational therapy practice setting Prefer red Qualifications Teaching experience Student interaction as clinical instructor or coordinator Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University is committed to promoting a culture of equity and inclusion among students, staff, and faculty. The university does not discriminate on the basis sex, gender, nor does the university discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, color, age, disability, religion, veteran’s status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. All correspondence relating to the position of Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Administration & Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled. Salary range is $80,000 – $90,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/psychiatric-mental-health-nurse-practitioner-faculty-full-or-part-time-assistant-associate-professor/": {
      "title": "Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Faculty (Full- or Part – Time; Assistant/Associate Professor)",
      "description": "Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Faculty (Full- or Part – Time; Assistant/Associate Professor) — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Faculty (Full- or Part – Time; Assistant/Associate Professor) Position Summary: Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences at Mary Baldwin University invites applications for the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) Faculty position with an anticipated start date of January 2027. This is a 12-month, full- or part-time faculty appointment in the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) Program within the School of Nursing at Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences. The faculty member teaches didactic, simulation, and clinical courses in the graduate PMHNP curriculum; advises and mentors students; and contributes to curriculum development, program evaluation, and continuous quality improvement. Teaching may include online, hybrid, and in-person instruction, including required on-campus learning experiences. Responsibilities and service expectations are adjusted proportionately to the faculty member’s contracted effort. Required Qualifications Graduate degree in nursing from an institutionally accredited institution and an accredited nursing program. Current national certification as a Psychiatric-Mental Health Nurse Practitioner across the lifespan (PMHNP-BC) through the American Nurses Credentialing Center. Current, unencumbered RN and APRN licensure with prescriptive authority in the Commonwealth of Virginia, or eligibility to obtain required Virginia licensure before the appointment begins. Current clinical competence and recent practice experience as a PMHNP; a minimum of three years of PMHNP clinical practice is preferred. Ability to teach graduate psychiatric mental health nursing content and evaluate student performance in didactic and clinical settings. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and organizational skills, with the ability to advise and mentor a diverse graduate student population. Ability to use—or willingness to learn—online and hybrid instructional technologies, including a learning management system, videoconferencing, and virtual learning tools. Doctoral degree: An earned DNP, PhD in Nursing, or related doctoral degree is preferred and may be required for appointment at certain ranks. Candidates with an MSN and substantial PMHNP clinical expertise may be considered consistent with university faculty qualification requirements. National certification: Current ANCC certification as a Psychiatric-Mental Health Nurse Practitioner across the lifespan (PMHNP-BC). Licensure: Active, unencumbered RN and APRN licensure with prescriptive authority in Virginia, or eligibility to obtain such licensure. Clinical experience: Current clinical competence and recent PMHNP practice experience; at least three years of PMHNP practice is preferred. Prefer red Qualifications Doctoral preparation in nursing or a closely related field. Graduate-level teaching experience, particularly in a PMHNP or other advanced practice nursing program. Experience with online and hybrid course delivery, learning management systems, instructional technology, and virtual or simulation-based learning. Experience with curriculum development, student assessment, clinical education, program evaluation, accreditation, or continuous quality improvement. Formal preparation or professional development in teaching, curriculum design, simulation, clinical precepting, or nursing education. Experience providing psychiatric mental health care to diverse or underserved populations and working within interprofessional care teams. Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University is committed to promoting a culture of equity and inclusion Mary Baldwin University is committed to promoting a culture of equity and inclusion among students, staff, and faculty. The university does not discriminate on the basis sex, gender, nor does the university discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, color, age, disability, religion, veteran’s status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. All correspondence relating to the position of PMHNP faculty should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Administration & Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled. Annual Salary is $110,000 #LI-DNI Annual Salary is $110,000#LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/assistant-associate-full-professor-of-social-work/": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor of Social Work",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor of Social Work — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Assistant / Associate / Full Professor of Social Work Position Summary: Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences at Mary Baldwin University invites applications for the Assistant/ Associate / Full Professor of Social Work position beginning with an anticipated start date of July 2027. We seek an experienced, dynamic social work educator to join the founding faculty team as we launch our new online MSW program. This position will teach, advise students, and play a major role in developing new courses, program processes, and policies. We currently have CSWE “pre-candidacy” status, with a first cohort starting in Spring 2027 as we roll out an innovative, “high touch”, student-centered, relationally based online learning approach to preparing outstanding advanced generalist social workers. The ideal candidate will enjoy the creative work of program development and will have a strong commitment to engaging and supporting the success of students from diverse backgrounds while strengthening meaningful connections with our broader practice community. This position is a full-time, renewable, 12-month position (no institutional tenure system) in Mary Baldwin University’s thriving Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences, serving the beautiful Shenandoah Valley region of Virginia. Required Qualifications Prior experience teaching at the MSW level 3+ years of post-MSW practice experience Expertise to teach Advanced Generalist practice courses in selected areas Earned MSW from A CSWE accredited program Prefer red Qualifications Curriculum and course development experience PhD/DSW Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University is committed to promoting a culture of equity and inclusion among students, staff, and faculty. The university does not discriminate on the basis sex, gender, nor does the university discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, color, age, disability, religion, veteran’s status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. All correspondence relating to the position of Social Work faculty should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Administration & Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled. Salary range is $65,000 – $75,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Annual Salary is $110,000#LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/housekeeper-2/": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Housekeeper — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Housekeeper Position Summary: Mary Baldwin University currently has positions available for Housekeepers.  Reporting to the Custodial Services Supervisor, this position provides general cleaning services and is a full-time, 40 hours per week position with benefits.  Rate of pay is $15 an hour. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Sweeping, dust/wet mopping, and vacuuming of floors Cleaning of offices and residence halls, including common areas Cleaning of restrooms, including fixtures, dispensers, toilets, showers/tubs Trash collection in offices/residence halls Other duties as assigned Minimum qualifications Knowledge of basic cleaning procedures and ability to follow written and oral instructions Previous experience cleaning in a university or institutional setting preferred, but not required Must be able to lift/carry items weighing up to 20 lbs. Valid driver’s license To Apply: Interested candidates may apply by sending a resume to Misty Miller, Housekeeping Supervisor, at mmiller@marybaldwin.edu , or complete an application at the MBU Facilities Office at 318 Prospect St., Staunton, VA 24401 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
