    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/groundskeeper-campus-support/": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper/Campus Support",
      "description": "Groundskeeper/Campus Support — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Groundskeeper/Campus Support Position Summary: Mary Baldwin University is seeking proactive and energetic individuals for the position of Groundskeeper/Campus Support. Reporting to the Maintenance & Grounds Supervisor, this is a 40 hours per week, full-time position with benefits.  Pay rate is $15 per hour. Overview of Position Groundskeeper duties include mowing, weeding, trimming, planting, trash removal, mulching, and snow removal.  Campus Support duties include set-up for campus events, delivery of supplies and equipment, and moving furniture. Groundskeepers work primarily outside, in all seasons and weather.  As essential personnel, work may be required occasionally on weekends and when the University is closed due to inclement weather. Minimum qualifications High school diploma or equivalent preferred. Valid Driver’s License and good driving record required. Heavy physical labor is involved, so must be able to lift and carry at least 50 lbs. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively. Must pass a background check. To Apply: Interested applicants may submit a resume to bkwhetzel@marybaldwin.edu or complete an application, which can be obtained at the Facilities Management Office at 318 Prospect St. Staunton, VA 24401. For more information, call 540-887-7209. #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/e-resources-and-discovery-librarian/": {
      "title": "E-Resources and Discovery Librarian",
      "description": "E-Resources and Discovery Librarian — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin E-Resources and Discovery Librarian Position Summary: Mary Baldwin University is currently seeking applicants for the position of E-Resources and Discovery Librarian in the Martha S. Grafton Library.  The Martha S. Grafton Library of Mary Baldwin University fosters academic success by providing information resources, learner-centered services and experiences, and welcoming spaces that facilitate lifelong learning, collaboration, and innovation. Position Summary This position coordinates interlibrary loan services and provides research discovery and assistance to students and faculty across all programs. This position facilitates the curation, maintenance, and promotion of e-resources, including management of the library’s website through LibGuides. This position delivers in-person and virtual reference assistance and provides instruction in how to find, critically evaluate, and effectively use a variety of information sources. Primary Responsibilities Coordinate the borrowing and lending of materials using the OCLC WorldShare system. Explore, recommend, and implement new resource sharing initiatives to improve customer service. Manage access to e-resources, including within the library’s website, and resolve issues locally and with database vendors. Collect usage statistics on a regular basis. Connect partners and resources across the institution and beyond in the exploration of academic and creative scholarship, including the use of OER and digital archives. Manage the library’s institutional repository with ContentDM. Participate with other library staff in ongoing collection evaluation. Produce regular and ad hoc reports in support of demand-driven collection development and resource sharing. Continue to develop professionally through active participation in professional associations and through other interdisciplinary activities. Requirements ALA-accredited Master’s degree in Library/Information Science or a related advanced degree. Fluency managing e-resources. Demonstrated reference and teaching experience. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation. Experience supporting digital scholarship in a library or research setting preferred. To Apply: Interested applicants may submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three references to Carol Creager, University Librarian, at ccreager@marybaldwin.edu . Annual Salary:  $50,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/senior-engineering-technician/": {
      "title": "Senior Engineering Technician",
      "description": "Senior Engineering Technician — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Senior Engineering Technician Position Summary: Mary Baldwin University is currently seeking applicants for the position of Senior Engineering Technician.  This is an hourly, non-exempt position.  Hourly rate is $29.00. Position Summary The Senior Engineering Technician is a highly skilled, experienced trades professional responsible for independently diagnosing, prioritizing, and completing complex maintenance and repair work across campus systems. Reporting to the Director of Facilities, this role serves as a technical resource and field leader, supporting HVAC, plumbing, and general maintenance operations, while collaborating with Facilities leadership and team members to ensure safe, code-compliant, and efficient work. This position does not include supervisor responsibilities, but requires high level of accountability, decision making, and professionalism in daily operations. Primary Responsibilities Technical Expertise and Work Execution Work Prioritization & Ownership Independently assess, prioritize, and complete assigned work orders Make real-time decisions based on urgency, safety, and operational impact Communicate with Facilities leadership when priorities conflict or escalation is needed Maintain accurate and timely documentation of completed work Vendor Coordination Identify when external vendors are required for specialized or large-scale work Coordinate with Facilities Operations for vendor engagement, scheduling, and access Serve as an onsite-point of contact to ensure work meets expectations and standards Apprenticeship & Team Support Support the Engineer Apprentice Program by providing guidance, hands-on training, and knowledge sharing Model proper techniques, safety practices, and knowledge sharing Assist team member across the Facilities team during high-demand periods Customer Service Interact professionally with campus partners, providing clear communication on work status and timeliness Represent Facilities as a responsive, professional, solutions-oriented team Safety & Compliance Follow and enforce all safety procedures, including PPE usage Ensure all work is completed in compliance with applicable codes and regulations Identify and report hazards, near misses, and safety concerns Support a proactive and accountable safety culture Core Expectations Independent Operator Sound Judgement Knows when to handle and issue independently or escalate to higher Understands limits and calls for support when needed Team-Oriented Supports team success over individual preference Avoids “that’s not my job” mindset Technical Leader Qualifications Required HVAC certification (EPA or equivalent) Demonstrated experience in facilities maintenance or skilled trades Working knowledge of plumbing and general maintenance sys Ability to work independently and prioritize tasks effectively Preferred Experience in institutional or campus environments Experience supporting or mentoring junior staff or apprentices Familiarity with work order systems and PM programs To Apply: Interested candidates may apply by sending a resume to Hannah Gazmen, Director of Facilities, at hcgazmen@marybaldwin.edu . #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/assistant-director-of-student-accounts/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Accounts",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Student Accounts — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Assistant Director of Student Accounts Position Summary: The Assistant Director for Student Accounts provides leadership and operational oversight for the Student Accounts staff and functions including customer service, student accounts billing, invoicing, training, compliance, and account collections. This role serves as a key leader within the Student Financial Services team by supporting quality customer service, accuracy, consistency, and continuous improvement of the departmental operations while ensuring compliance with institutional, federal, and state requirements. This is a salaried, exempt position.  Annual salary: $58,000 Primary Responsibilities Provide leadership and operational oversight for the Student Accounts team Supervise student accounts team by providing day-to-day operational support, training, and ensuring adequate office coverage Maintain accuracy of student tuition and fee accounts for all students (current and incoming) Assist with student billing process including managing charge tables, adjustments, and discounts Manage the 1098-T annual process including forms testing, reviewing, and distributing the forms via mail or online Oversee internal and 3 rd party collection efforts ensuring timely processing and compliance with applicable requirements Manage the initial and/or recurring system set up for 3 rd party vendors including but not limited to payment plans, payments, and book vouchers Assist with maintaining student account policies, procedures, webpages, forms, and documents Serve as an approver for fiscal processes within student accounts including but not limited to posting disbursements and processing journal entries Serve as the point of contact for complex account issues and independently research and identify potential resolution Assist with developing communication timeline including student billing, invoices, book vouchers, payment plans and other important deadlines Assist with internal and external audit requirements and coordinates successful annual fiscal close procedures in compliance with Finance Develop strong partnerships with other departments within the university focused on strong collaborative relationships focused on continuous improvement efforts Special projects or duties as assigned Required Qualifications and Experience Bachelor’s degree in Business, Management, Accounting, Finance or related field. A minimum of 3-5 years of prior supervisory experience in student financial services, student accounts, financial aid, or similar field. Knowledge of applying federal and state regulations as it pertains to financial industries such as student accounts and financial aid. Knowledge of accounting principles, collection procedures, computerized accounting and billing systems. Demonstrated experience developing and implementing business process improvements. Background in preparing operational reports, analyzing data, and audits Strong organizational skills with ability to prioritize and handle multiple tasks and work under pressure. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite products, including a working knowledge of Microsoft Excel spreadsheets and advanced Excel formulas. To Apply: Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest and resume to Jill Gable, Associate Vice President Enrollment Management, Student Financial Services at jegable@marybaldwin.edu . #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/student-accounts-administrator/": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Administrator",
      "description": "Student Accounts Administrator — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Student Accounts Administrator Position Summary: The Student Accounts Administrator plays a key role in managing the day-to-day operations of the Student Accounts Department by ensuring strong financial processes to enable student success and institutional effectiveness. Under general supervision, the student accounts coordinator completes a full range of complex student finance and cashiering related functions utilizing student billing and payment authorization systems. The student accounts administrator is responsible for providing world class service delivery while guiding students through the payment plan set up process and management of their student finance account. This is an hourly, non-exempt position.  Hourly rate: $26.00 Primary Responsibilities Support student accounts operations including billing, payment processing, book vouchers, refunds, and collections Prepare, review for accuracy, and provide billing statements to students Deliver excellent customer service by providing direct student and/or parent support in managing student accounts by explaining tuition, fees, payment options, and related charges Manage the student refund process by preparing, reviewing, and entering the refunds for processing Manage the day-to-day AR collections efforts including but not limited to tracking and monitoring student accounts Assist with preparing AR reports including aging summaries and collection performance metrics Coordinate with vendors and internal departments to resolve student billing and payment discrepancies Manage student withdrawals and billing adjustments as needed Input daily cash receipts utilizing standard operating procedures Assist with monthly reconciliations of bank records, student aid funds, and other accounts as requested Prepare billing invoices for a variety of programs including employer reimbursements, international colleges and programs, 529 Plans, military programs, etc. Process and ensure timely distribution of the annual 1098-T tuition tax forms Manage student account hold process in alignment with established policies and procedures Prepare and enter various fiscal processes including but not limited to entering journal entries into the financial system Collaborate with the office of Student Engagement to accurately bill room and board charges Apply rules, regulations, procedures, and guidelines governing financial aid, student billing and debt collections Partner with other departments on campus to build strong collaborative relationships focused on continuous improvement efforts Special projects or duties as assigned. Required Qualifications and Experience Associate degree in finance, accounting, or related math or business field. A minimum of two years of experience in accounts receivable, collections, higher education finance, or related field. Strong organizational skills with ability to prioritize and handle multiple tasks and work under pressure. Ability to manage a high volume of inquiries via email, phone, and in person. Exceptional oral and written communication skills. Strong attention to details and accuracy of maintaining financial related data. Proficient computer skills, including knowledge with Google Suite, Adobe, and Microsoft Office. Knowledge of accounting principles, collection procedures, computerized accounting and student billing systems. To Apply: Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest and resume to Jill Gable, Associate Vice President Enrollment Management, Student Financial Services at jegable@marybaldwin.edu . #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Athletics Accreditation Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    }
